/-!
# SL₃ recognition for G.9.3: established branches and reductions

The smallest-field module classification is complete, including the actual
component isomorphism and the kernel of its quotient map. The natural
recognition implication over every binary field proves that the component
is SL₃, and the tensor-orbit arithmetic isolates the half-field exception.
The automorphism-rank reduction retains the actual central quotient.
The twisted-tensor kernel calculation distinguishes PSL₃(4) from SL₃(16),
including dual modules, once the descended action is identified.

The general restricted-factor classification, its Frobenius-field descent,
and the larger-field automorphism upper bound remain prerequisites. In
particular this module does not yet assert exhaustive G.9.3(8),(17).

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, G.9.3, printed pp.354,356--357; GLS III,
2.8.6, 2.8.8 and 2.8.10(c).
-/
